      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "mms_steady_dirichlet_central",
          "description": "Exact unforced advection-diffusion solution u*(x,t) = e^{2x} + e^{-lambda t} e^{x} sin(pi x) with c = 1, nu = 1/2, lambda = 5.434802200544679, fixed-value walls gL = 1, gR = e^2. Derivation: the steady mode e^{2x} (nonzero walls) and the decaying first Dirichlet eigenfunction e^{-lambda t} e^{x} sin(pi x) (homogeneous walls) each solve u_t = -c u_x + nu u_xx exactly, so u* is an exact solution and the discrete drift is the pure spatial truncation of the two operators — dominated by the advective central_D1_dirichlet_bc term (metadata.description). The diffusion makes the two-sided fixed-value problem well posed and stable; the decay is parabolic, so boundary truncation stays global O(dx^2). References evaluate at cell centers x_i = 0 + (i - 1/2)/N, spelled inline per esm-spec 6.6.5 (build-time evaluation folds literals and metaparameters only). The t=0 assertion pins the ic wiring (reference equals the initial field). The t=0.05 assertion bounds the truncation-driven error against the exact reference (well under the bound at the default N=64, falling at order 2). Exact per-resolution errors are pinned in tests/conformance/convergence/advection_1d_dirichlet_central/golden/errors.json.",
